    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py` and it works: the tests pass and an offline check returned the expected values.\n\n```python\nresponse = client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n    model=MODEL, max_tokens=256, messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n)\nmessage = response.parse()\nreturn {\n    \"request_id\": response.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n    \"raw_body\": response.text(),\n    \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n}\n```\n\n**A version-specific detail:** in the pinned `anthropic==1.8.0`, `text()` on a raw response is a method, not a property as in older SDKs. The raw response class changed in 1.x. I checked this in the Context7 migration notes and in the installed `_response.py`. Writing it the old way (`response.text`) would put a bound method into `raw_body` instead of the JSON text.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `pytest -q`: 1 passed. The existing test only checks that `MODEL` is set, so it doesn't exercise this function.\n- I ran a smoke test against a fake HTTP endpoint (httpx2's `MockTransport`) that returned a `request-id` header and two text blocks. The result was `request_id == \"req_abc\"`, `answer == \"Hello\"`, and `raw_body` exactly matched the body sent.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete the smoke-test script because the `rm` command needed approval. Please delete `_smoke_audit.py` from the project root, or keep it as a starting point for a real test."
